{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>So I took the heads of your tribes.</b> I drew them — happy are you: upon whom have you come to be appointed? Upon the children of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, upon people who were called brothers and friends, portion and inheritance, and every term of endearment (ibid.)." "<b>Men who are wise and knowing.</b> But men of understanding I did not find. This is one of seven qualities that Jethro said to Moses, and he found only three: <b>men</b> — righteous, <b>wise, and knowing</b> (ibid.)." "<b>Heads over you.</b> That you treat them with honor — first in purchase, first in sale, first in business dealings: the last one enters and the first one goes out (ibid.)." "<b>Officers of thousands.</b> One appointed over a thousand." "<b>Officers of hundreds.</b> One appointed over a hundred." "<b>And officers.</b> I appointed over you <b>for your tribes</b> — these are the ones who bind and strike with a strap at the word of the judges (see there)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:29.485658905Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}